### Guide §5.5 Advanced JPA. VS Code REST Client syntax: click "Send Request" above each request.
### Start the app with the dev profile (demo authors, books, members and loans):
###   ./mvnw -pl spring-app spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.profiles=dev
### The console shows every SQL statement. Ids and statuses assume the demo data on an empty
### database, and a first run of this file: reset with docker compose -f spring-app/compose.yaml down -v
### "# @name x" names a request, so later ones can use {{x.response.body.id}}.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### A page of books, sorted by title (200, 10 books). Three SQL statements, whatever the page size:
### the page, the active loans grouped by book, then the authors of all its books (... where book_id = any (?))
GET {{host}}/api/books

### Page 1 (zero-based) of 3, newest first (200). With more rows than one page, Spring Data also
### sends a select count(...) for totalElements
GET {{host}}/api/books?page=1&size=3&sort=publishedYear,desc

### Jane Austen's books (200, 3 books): a join on book_authors
GET {{host}}/api/books?authorId=3

### A size above 100 is clamped (200, "size": 100)
GET {{host}}/api/books?size=500

### Not a sortable property (400, "Cannot sort by 'popularity'. Sortable: ...")
GET {{host}}/api/books?sort=popularity

### A real path, but through a collection: a join would duplicate rows across pages (400)
GET {{host}}/api/books?sort=authors.name

### Dune (200): 3 copies, 1 on loan to Ada, so availableCopies 2. One SELECT with a left join to
### the authors (the entity graph), then the loan count
GET {{host}}/api/books/1

### Authors, sorted by name (200)
GET {{host}}/api/authors

### Frank Herbert's books (200: Dune, Dune Messiah). An interface projection: select id, title only
GET {{host}}/api/authors/1/books

### Frank Herbert still has books (409)
DELETE {{host}}/api/authors/1

### Two new authors (201 each), then one book by both
# @name pratchett
POST {{host}}/api/authors
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Terry Pratchett", "birthYear": 1948}

###
# @name gaiman
POST {{host}}/api/authors
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Neil Gaiman", "birthYear": 1960}

### Good Omens by both (201; authors sorted by name). SQL: insert into books, then one insert into
### book_authors per author
POST {{host}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{"isbn": "9780060853983", "title": "Good Omens", "publishedYear": 1990, "totalCopies": 2,
 "authorIds": [{{pratchett.response.body.id}}, {{gaiman.response.body.id}}]}

### An author id that does not exist (404, "Author 999 not found")
POST {{host}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{"isbn": "9780547928227", "title": "The Hobbit", "publishedYear": 1937, "totalCopies": 1, "authorIds": [999]}

### A new member (201; the email is stored lowercase)
POST {{host}}/api/members
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "Hedy@Library.test", "fullName": "Hedy Lamarr"}

### The same email in another case (409)
POST {{host}}/api/members
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "hedy@library.TEST", "fullName": "Someone else"}

### The Dispossessed has one copy, and Alan has it (409, "Book 4 has no available copies")
POST {{host}}/api/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{"bookId": 4, "memberId": 1}

### Grace borrows Dune (201): due today + 14 days
# @name loan
POST {{host}}/api/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{"bookId": 1, "memberId": 3}

### Grace's active loans (200: Pale Blue Dot, overdue, and Dune). One SELECT joins the books
GET {{host}}/api/loans?memberId=3&active=true

### Return it (200, returnedAt set)
POST {{host}}/api/loans/{{loan.response.body.id}}/return

### Return it again (409, "... was already returned")
POST {{host}}/api/loans/{{loan.response.body.id}}/return

### Dune has loans, so it cannot be deleted (409)
DELETE {{host}}/api/books/1

### Returned loans (200: Ada's Emma and Grace's Dune)
GET {{host}}/api/loans?active=false
